==Strategy==
Codename "Red Riding" makes her grand return in this stage, which plays out pretty similarly to [[Learned to Love]]. Given that "Red Riding" spawns fairly quickly, it is vital to farm the Doge Darks and the Celeboodle with [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] to get enough money to spawn a Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]; your win condition is killing "Red Riding" before the 200% Cosmic Cyclone arrives. You do, however need to let her advance a little bit from the base, or Cosmic Cyclone will kill A. Bahamut before he can take down the boss. Alongside fast units like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], Can Can Cat, and [[Jetpack Cat (Rare Cat)|Jetpack]] in the event that Cosmic Cyclone arrives. Mina will ideally fall right as the Cosmic Cyclone reaches you. If you need a bit more time, you can use the [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt]] Cannon to buy yourself a few extra seconds and kill "Red Riding". Once Mina goes down, your new goal is killing Cosmic Cyclone. Because of this, make sure to run both [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] and [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]] for the Owlbrowley and Darkmadillo that spawns later on. Once Cosmic Cyclone goes down, you've cleared the stage.

==Trivia==
*The "Love" in Dozing Love is likely a reference to [[Learned to Love]], where [[Codename "Red Riding"]] made her first appearance. Their names are closer in [[BCJP]], with Dozing Love being Nemuritate no Ai (眠りたての愛, "Freshly Asleep Love") and Learned to Love being Oboetate no Ai (おぼたての愛, "Freshly Learned Love" or "Freshly Remembered Love").

